        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7752d42d-8b26-564d-8982-b4942fc147e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Tron; The Million Dollar Duck; Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure\n- People: Steven Lisberger; Bonnie MacBird; Jeff Bridges; Dan Shor\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Roles: Ram; Billy the Kid\n- Concepts: science fiction action-adventure film; comedy film; mainframe computer; golden eggs\n\nFacts:\n- The Million Dollar Duck, also titled The $1,000,000 Duck, is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- Tron is a 1982 American science fiction action-adventure film written and directed by Steven Lisberger and based on a story by Steven Lisberger and Bonnie MacBird.\n- Tron was produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- Jeff Bridges stars in Tron as a computer programmer who is transported inside the software world of a mainframe computer and interacts with programs while trying to escape.\n- Dan Shor is recognized for playing Ram in Tron (1982).\n- Dan Shor is also recognized for playing Billy the Kid in Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure (1989).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
